TITLE:: Pwindow
SUMMARY:: Lazy sliding windows over any source
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events>Patterns>Patternarium
RELATED:: Classes/Pscan, Classes/Pclump, Classes/Pslide

DESCRIPTION::
Yields fresh shallow Arrays of size items, advancing by step. Overlap, clumping and gaps are supported. Partial true emits one final incomplete window only when a new buffered item has arrived since the last full window. It never emits a trailing overlap by itself. No leading partial windows are produced unless the source is shorter than size. An indexed ring buffer uses O(size) storage. Each yielded Array costs O(size) to copy; advancing the buffer clears dropped references without shifting retained items. Gapped windows additionally consume step-size skipped values. Source termination returns the latest inval.

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: pattern
Source Pattern.
ARGUMENT:: size
Positive Integer, Function or Pattern evaluated once.
ARGUMENT:: step
Positive Integer, default 1; evaluated once.
ARGUMENT:: partial
Boolean, default false; evaluated once.

INSTANCEMETHODS::
METHOD:: storeArgs
Returns the constructor arguments for archive reconstruction.
METHOD:: embedInStream
Runs the stream protocol and returns the latest inval on termination.

EXAMPLES::
code::
Pwindow(Pseries(0, 1, 6), 3).asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pwindow / Value stream
var values = {
Pwindow(Pseries(0, 1, 6), 3).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \fmPiano, degree: if(x.isArray) { x } { x*2 }, dur: 0.22, amp: 0.06)
}.play;
)
::

SECTION:: Musical example
Load the example instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments:: first, then evaluate this block.
code::
(
Pbind(\instrument, \fmPiano, \degree, Pwindow(Pseries(0, 1, 16), 3, 2).collect(_.mean), \dur, 0.125).play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Moving mean
code::
Pwindow(Pseries(1, 1, 8), 3).collect(_.mean).asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: Pwindow / Moving mean
var values = {
Pwindow(Pseries(1, 1, 8), 3).collect(_.mean).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \fmPiano, degree: if(x.isArray) { x } { x*2 }, dur: 0.22, amp: 0.06)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Moving median
code::
Pwindow(Pseq([1, 9, 3, 2, 8]), 3).collect { |w| w.sort[1] }.asStream.all;
::

